# Reference substrate-authors allowlist.
#
# This file is a substrate-published reference template demonstrating
# the format the substrate-write-isolation pre-commit hook
# (governance-commons/reference/hooks/pre-commit) expects.
#
# Substrate-recommended consumer integration:
#   - Copy this file to the consumer's repo root as
#     `.substrate-authors`.
#   - Edit to list the substrate-author identities authorized to
#     write into governance-commons/.
#   - Each line is either an email address or a git user.name,
#     compared exact-match against `git config user.email` and
#     `git config user.name` at commit time.
#   - Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored.
#
# The substrate's own working copy of this allowlist (as used by
# the substrate-author for their own development of the substrate)
# is not shipped in the substrate; each consumer maintains their
# own. This file is illustrative only.

# Example identities (consumer edits):
# alice@example.com
# Alice Engineer
# bob@example.com
